      "id": "AG-QC-01.theorem-5-1",
      "title": "Two open sets and the connecting map",
      "lesson_id": "AG-QC-01",
      "reader": "docs/courses/AG-QC/cohomology-of-sheaves-on-ringed-spaces.html#5-two-open-sets-and-the-connecting-map",
      "source": "docs/courses/AG-QC/src/cohomology-of-sheaves-on-ringed-spaces.md",
      "source_sha256": "90c34f08aa0b7cf16ac7ba2bf950f049a8458df6c45feff866231af50780b977",
      "reader_sha256": "ebe9407afa807fc50f21b4ad20ead65531a1765c043efd6ca03027bdc181901e",
      "statement_html": "<p><strong>Theorem 5.1 (Mayer–Vietoris).</strong> If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\(X=U\\cup V\\)\">\\(X=U\\cup V\\)</span> is an open cover, there is a natural exact sequence\n<span class=\"math math-display\" data-tex=\"\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&amp;\\to H^0(X,\\mathcal F)\n\\to H^0(U,\\mathcal F)\\oplus H^0(V,\\mathcal F)\n\\to H^0(U\\cap V,\\mathcal F)\\\\\n&amp;\\to H^1(X,\\mathcal F)\n\\to H^1(U,\\mathcal F)\\oplus H^1(V,\\mathcal F)\n\\to H^1(U\\cap V,\\mathcal F)\\to\\cdots.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\">\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&amp;\\to H^0(X,\\mathcal F)\n\\to H^0(U,\\mathcal F)\\oplus H^0(V,\\mathcal F)\n\\to H^0(U\\cap V,\\mathcal F)\\\\\n&amp;\\to H^1(X,\\mathcal F)\n\\to H^1(U,\\mathcal F)\\oplus H^1(V,\\mathcal F)\n\\to H^1(U\\cap V,\\mathcal F)\\to\\cdots.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]</span>\nThe map from the two opens to their intersection is restriction from <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\(U\\)\">\\(U\\)</span> minus restriction from <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\(V\\)\">\\(V\\)</span>.</p>",
      "availability": "statement_and_proof_present"
    },
    {
      "id": "AG-QC-02.theorem-2-1",
      "title": "A smaller complex without repeated indices",
      "lesson_id": "AG-QC-02",
      "reader": "docs/courses/AG-QC/cech-cohomology.html#2-a-smaller-complex-without-repeated-indices",
      "source": "docs/courses/AG-QC/src/cech-cohomology.md",
      "source_sha256": "63988581823cbb25c6f3678c41c9c743add99fe8753175922fb059e5972b5871",
      "reader_sha256": "bb671a20137ba6d2e09eb5010d65c5ccfb7238ac469be119796cd49ccf3a7c2e",
      "statement_html": "<p><strong>Theorem 2.1.</strong> The ordered and alternating complexes are isomorphic, and their inclusion into the full complex is a homotopy equivalence. No division by a factorial is involved.</p>",
      "availability": "statement_and_proof_present"
    },
    {
      "id": "AG-QC-02.theorem-3-2",
      "title": "Comparing overlaps with derived cohomology",
      "lesson_id": "AG-QC-02",
      "reader": "docs/courses/AG-QC/cech-cohomology.html#3-comparing-overlaps-with-derived-cohomology",
