      "source_sha256": "63988581823cbb25c6f3678c41c9c743add99fe8753175922fb059e5972b5871",
      "reader_sha256": "bb671a20137ba6d2e09eb5010d65c5ccfb7238ac469be119796cd49ccf3a7c2e",
      "statement_html": "<p><strong>Theorem 3.2 (acyclic covers).</strong> If <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\(H^q(U_{i_0\\ldots i_p},\\mathcal F)=0\\)\">\\(H^q(U_{i_0\\ldots i_p},\\mathcal F)=0\\)</span> for all <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\(q&gt;0\\)\">\\(q&gt;0\\)</span> and every nonempty finite intersection, then the natural comparison is an isomorphism\n<span class=\"math math-display\" data-tex=\"\\[\n\\check H^p(\\mathcal U,\\mathcal F)\\cong H^p(X,\\mathcal F)\n\\]\">\\[\n\\check H^p(\\mathcal U,\\mathcal F)\\cong H^p(X,\\mathcal F)\n\\]</span>\nfor every <span class=\"math\" data-tex=\"\\(p\\)\">\\(p\\)</span>.</p>",
